"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-10T06:29:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T08:48:57Z","closed_at":"2025-05-10T08:33:09Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in 4.4.1 and 4.5.dev3\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot Engine v4.5.dev3.official.55fc6e73f - https://godotengine.org Vulkan 1.3.280 - Forward+ - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe autocomplete and syntax highlighter make it seems that the enum type is in Scope, but in reality map to different types.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe following produces an error:\n```\nclass_name TEST extends Node\nenum Side {LEFT,RIGHT}\n\nfunc _ready():\n var my_enum:Side = Side.LEFT\n```\n\n> Cannot assign a value of type TEST.Side to variable \"my_enum\" with specified type Side.\n\n\nThe following does *not* produce an error:\n```\nclass_name TEST extends Node\nenum Side {LEFT,RIGHT}\n\nfunc _ready():\n var my_enum:TEST.Side = TEST.Side.LEFT\n```\nThis also doesn't produce an error\n```\nclass_name TEST extends Node\nenum Side {LEFT,RIGHT}\n\nfunc _ready():\n var my_enum:Side = TEST.Side.Left as Side\n```\n\nThe issue is that you can't create function local enums without creating a global namespace.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP is included in issue steps","closed_by":{"login":"BlackShift","id":5866818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjY4MTg=","avatar_url":"http